        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(macos): defer cookie import banner until inline browser opens",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where macOS app users could see the browser cookie-import banner while the embedded dashboard was still showing its Gateway connection or authentication screen. The automatic offer previously ran after app launch and every Gateway connection, before the inline browser was used.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe app now requests the automatic cookie-import offer only after the inline browser sidebar opens for the first time. Later sidebar opens do not request it again, while Settings -> General -> Browser login -> Import remains the explicit re-offer path.\n\nThis is the narrow timing follow-up to the inline banner introduced in #104591. AI-assisted; reviewed with the repository autoreview helper.\n\nCurrent `main` also had stale native translation handoff and runtime resources, which made the repository-wide native i18n gate fail for every native PR. This PR includes the canonical mechanical refresh so the bug fix can pass exact-head CI; no localization generator or runtime behavior changed.\n\nTwo additional current-`main` CI regressions are repaired in the same landing train: removal of an unused private MSteams helper left by #106279 and regeneration of the stale docs map.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe Gateway connection/authentication screen stays clear. Eligible local-Gateway users see the cookie-import offer when it becomes relevant: the first time they open the inline browser.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added a macOS smoke regression proving dashboard show does not request the offer, first inline-browser open requests it once, and later opens do not request it again.\n- `./scripts/format-swift.sh` - clean.\n- `./scripts/lint-swift.sh` - 0 violations.\n- Blacksmith Testbox through Crabbox `tbx_01kxdd0wnvn87yr581p5bjhh2z`: `corepack pnpm check:changed` - passed 5 routed Vitest shards and all changed-file gates.\n- Same Testbox: `corepack pnpm check:docs` - 0 Markdown errors, 0 broken links, docs map current.\n- Blacksmith Testbox through Crabbox `tbx_01kxdfgm0evpenkp6pfmqpa81v`: `native:i18n:check`, `android:i18n:check`, and `apple:i18n:check` - all passed after canonical generation (4,320 source entries).\n- Blacksmith Testbox through Crabbox `tbx_01kxdh3d9g5xhbj24w1t5tcmjx`: `corepack pnpm tsgo:extensions` and `corepack pnpm check:docs` - passed after repairing the current-`main` regressions.\n- Testbox Actions run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29239383423\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --stream-engine-output ...` - clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nVisual recording is not attached because this native timing change requires a signed macOS app profile; the PR's macOS Swift lane builds and runs the exact regression on a macOS runner.\n",
